-- RC2 - Material Balance EXPERT (advanced tier) goes deep. COMPLETES THE LADDER.
--
-- Inserts the ACTIVE academy_course_structures row for (mbal, advanced),
-- generated from src/content/courses/mbal/advanced/manifest.json rather than
-- hand-typed, and seeds the six module quiz banks plus the final exam. Answer
-- keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no client SELECT
-- policy.
--
-- Six modules, 25 lessons: the finite aquifer, Carter-Tracy, combination drive,
-- history matching, validation tiers, and the Expert reading.
--
-- Every numeric item traces to the RC2 truth digest or to the Expert
-- verification runs recorded in /root/rc-wip-mbal/EXPERT-VALUES*.txt, and
-- reproduces the live Expert capstone answer key: Dake Exercise 9.2 through
-- Carter-Tracy with the mapped finite aquifer returning OOIP 307.221409553720
-- MMSTB and cumulative influx 88.0645883139400 MMrb, the bounded-circle
-- dimensionless pressure 9.30886079703705 at reD 5 and tD 100, and Ahmed
-- Example 11-1 giving We 411281.250000001 bbl with a water drive index of
-- 0.211250877090399 and four indices summing to 1 under the net-withdrawal
-- convention.
--
-- TIER POSITIONING: the Associate tier owns the tank, the terms, the straight
-- line, drive indices and the volumetrics reconciliation; the Professional tier
-- owns the aquifer diagnostic, the pot model, Fetkovich, gas p/z and PVT
-- precedence. This tier owns what neither can reach: that the repo holds THREE
-- representations of the infinite-acting case and the graded Dake number comes
-- from a different code path than the graded pD; Carter-Tracy as an
-- approximation to superposition; combination drive and the denominator
-- convention that decides whether the indices close; history matching, where an
-- eight-fold better pressure fit moves the oil in place twenty million barrels
-- further from the published answer; and validation tiers, where the provenance
-- string for this very path still records numbers the engine no longer returns.
--
-- THE TIER'S SHARPEST LESSON, and it completes the pair the tiers below set up
-- ("a straight line does not validate your constants", "a high R-squared does
-- not validate your model"): a benchmark badge does not validate your run. The
-- Dake history with the aquifer term removed comes back benchmark_verified,
-- silent, at R-squared 0.999317934436751, and 225.366832034673 MMSTB above the
-- Carter-Tracy answer.
--
-- LADDER: an advanced enrolment needs an unrevoked PROFESSIONAL certificate on
-- the SAME app. P3b probes prove the mbal Associate and Professional tiers
-- undisturbed at 132 questions each.
--
-- Bank QA before seeding: correct-option length rank 0 and rank 3 each at or
-- below 30 percent on all seven served pools, within-pool and cross-bank
-- duplicate sweeps clean, no true synonym option pairs, keys balanced and
-- non-cyclic, no em or en dashes, and no capstone field grading a topic a lower
-- tier owns.
--
-- Numeric provenance before seeding: every literal a question ASSERTS (prompt,
-- correct option, explanation) was re-derived from the central engines in Node
-- by an independent verification pass written after the banks
-- (rc2_expert_verify*.mjs). It found and fixed six defects: a distractor that
-- was true of the engine's own march, a mixed-spacing comparison of the two
-- Carter-Tracy implementations, a percentage described as a distance change
-- when it was a relative move, two options that differed only in where a
-- bracket fell, an "only" that ignored the gas cap index, and fourteen
-- literals computed by arithmetic on printed 15-figure values rather than on
-- the raw engine doubles.
-- ============================================================================

values ('mbal', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-finite-aquifer","title":"The Finite Aquifer","lesson_keys":["l01-two-solution-families","l02-the-line-source-limit","l03-pseudo-steady-state","l04-reading-the-pd-table","l05-why-finite-matters"]},{"key":"m02-carter-tracy","title":"Carter-Tracy","lesson_keys":["l01-the-superposition-problem","l02-the-carter-tracy-step","l03-dake-9-2","l04-the-benchmark-verdict"]},{"key":"m03-combination-drive","title":"Combination Drive","lesson_keys":["l01-more-than-one-mechanism","l02-the-gas-cap-term","l03-ahmed-11-1","l04-apportioning-the-drive"]},{"key":"m04-history-matching","title":"History Matching","lesson_keys":["l01-what-matching-means","l02-parameters-and-bounds","l03-the-danger-of-freedom","l04-matching-honestly"]},{"key":"m05-validation-tiers","title":"Validation Tiers","lesson_keys":["l01-benchmark-versus-method","l02-what-a-tier-claims","l03-warnings-versus-tiers","l04-reading-the-provenance"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-workflow","l02-capstone-walkthrough","l03-the-reserves-memo","l04-onward-on-the-reservoir-path"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
